{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.rj_canonical_inner_product","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rj_canonical_inner_product","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Module","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Adjoin.Basic"],"declarations":48,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.markov3_unique_adjoin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.markov3_unique_adjoin","kind":"theorem","line":533,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L533-L546","doc":"**Markov uniqueness on the whole of `H₃`** (part (ii) at `r = 3`): two linear\nfunctionals satisfying the Markov conditions for the same `z` agree on every\nelement of the subalgebra generated by `s₁, s₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.exists_eval_of_mem_adjoin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.exists_eval_of_mem_adjoin","kind":"theorem","line":504,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L504-L531","doc":"Every element of the subalgebra generated by `s₁, s₂` is the evaluation of\nsome coordinate vector, i.e. `{1, s₁, s₂, s₁s₂, s₂s₁, s₁s₂s₁}` spans it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_smul","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L501-L502","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_add","kind":"theorem","line":498,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L498-L499","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.smul","kind":"def","line":490,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L490-L492","doc":"Coordinate-wise scalar multiple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.add","kind":"def","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L486-L488","doc":"Coordinate-wise sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h3_markov_rossoJones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h3_markov_rossoJones","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L465-L481","doc":"**Part (iii) at `r = 3` for every Markov trace.** In any `R`-algebra `A`\nwith `s₁, s₂` satisfying the Hecke and braid relations, any linear functional\nsatisfying the convention-D Markov conditions has\n`[2]³ · t((s₁s₂)ˢ) = [4] q^{2s} + [2]·χ(s)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h3Trace_rossoJones_coprime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h3Trace_rossoJones_coprime","kind":"theorem","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L455-L462","doc":"**Torus knots `τ(3, s)`, `3 ∤ s`**: the block's formula\n`[r+1] q^{s(r−1)} − [r−1] q^{s(r−3)}` at `r = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h3Trace_rossoJones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h3Trace_rossoJones","kind":"theorem","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L412-L452","doc":"**Rosso–Jones at `r = 3`, every `s`**, in `H₃(q)` with the convention-D\nMarkov trace: `[2]³ · tr_M((σ₁σ₂)ˢ) = [4] q^{2s} + [2] · χ(s)`, where\n`χ(s) = 2` if `3 ∣ s` and `−1` otherwise (the character of `γˢ` on the\ntwo-row block `(2,1)`, whose sl₂ dimension is `[2]`; the `(1³)` block carries\nweight `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h3_residual_fullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h3_residual_fullTwist","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L397-L409","doc":"The residual `g = [2]³·tr_M − [4]·triv` is invariant under the full twist\n`γ³ = Δ²`: `Δ²` acts by `1` on the two-row block `(2,1)` and the Ocneanu weight\nof the three-row block `(1³)` is `0` under convention D. Proved as an identity\nin the six coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.qIntBal_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.qIntBal_four","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L390-L394","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.triv_gammaPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.triv_gammaPow","kind":"theorem","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L382-L386","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.triv_rs2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.triv_rs2","kind":"theorem","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L378-L380","doc":"The trivial character is multiplicative along `σ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.triv_rs1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.triv_rs1","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L374-L376","doc":"The trivial character is multiplicative along `σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.markov3_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.markov3_unique","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L347-L370","doc":"**Markov uniqueness on `H₃`.** Any `R`-linear functional `t` with `t 1 = 1`,\n`t s₁ = z`, `t(xy) = t(yx)`, and the Markov property `t(x s₂) = z t(x)` for\n`x ∈ H₂ = span{1, s₁}` takes the value `markovTr q z v` on `eval v`. In\nparticular it is unique given `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_gammaPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_gammaPow","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L339-L344","doc":"`γˢ = (s₁s₂)ˢ` is the evaluation of `gammaPow q s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_rs2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_rs2","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L330-L337","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_rs1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval_rs1","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L318-L325","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.eval","kind":"def","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L308-L311","doc":"Evaluation of coordinates in an `R`-algebra with chosen `s₁, s₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.triv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.triv","kind":"def","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L300-L302","doc":"The trivial character `σᵢ ↦ q`, read on coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.markovTr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.markovTr","kind":"def","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L294-L298","doc":"The Markov trace on the basis, as forced by the Markov conditions\n(`markov3_unique`): `tr(1) = 1`, `tr(σᵢ) = z`, `tr(σ₁σ₂) = tr(σ₂σ₁) = z²`,\n`tr(σ₁σ₂σ₁) = z·(1 + (q − q⁻¹) z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.gammaPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.gammaPow","kind":"def","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L289-L292","doc":"Coordinates of `γˢ`, `γ = σ₁σ₂` (the `(3, s)` torus braid). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.one","kind":"def","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L286-L287","doc":"The unit `1 ∈ H₃(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.rs2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.rs2","kind":"def","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L279-L284","doc":"Right multiplication by `σ₂`: `σ₂·σ₂ = (q−q⁻¹)σ₂ + 1`,\n`σ₁σ₂·σ₂ = (q−q⁻¹)σ₁σ₂ + σ₁`, `σ₂σ₁·σ₂ = σ₁σ₂σ₁` (braid),\n`σ₁σ₂σ₁·σ₂ = (q−q⁻¹)σ₁σ₂σ₁ + σ₂σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.rs1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.rs1","kind":"def","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L273-L277","doc":"Right multiplication by `σ₁`: `σ₁·σ₁ = (q−q⁻¹)σ₁ + 1`,\n`σ₂σ₁·σ₁ = (q−q⁻¹)σ₂σ₁ + σ₂`, `σ₁σ₂σ₁·σ₁ = (q−q⁻¹)σ₁σ₂σ₁ + σ₁σ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.aba","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.aba","kind":"def","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L269-L269","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.ba","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.ba","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L268-L268","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.ab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.ab","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L267-L267","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.b","kind":"def","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L266-L266","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.a","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L265-L265","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.e","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L264-L264","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3.mk","kind":"ctor","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L263-L263","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.H3","kind":"structure","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L261-L269","doc":"Coordinates of an element of `H₃(q)` in the basis\n`{1, σ₁, σ₂, σ₁σ₂, σ₂σ₁, σ₁σ₂σ₁}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.rj_canonical_inner_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.rj_canonical_inner_product","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L236-L245","doc":"**Top-level bundle** for `prop:rj-canonical-inner-product`, the part that is\nformalised: the Markov parameter is `z_D`, the surviving hook dimensions are\n`[r+1]` and `[r−1]`, and part (iii) holds at `r = 2` for every `s`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:rj-canonical-inner-product","label":"prop:rj-canonical-inner-product","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/rj-canonical-inner-product.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.old_form_ii_false_r2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.old_form_ii_false_r2","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L213-L234","doc":"The field formerly carried as `claim_unique_up_to_scalar` — every diagonal\nform normalised at the trivial class is a scalar multiple of `d_λ` — fails at\n`r = 2` (classes `(2) ↦ 0`, `(1,1) ↦ 1`, `d = ([3], [1])`): the diagonal form\n`diag(1, 0)` is not a multiple of it. A diagonal form has one free entry per\ntwo-row class; only the Markov trace (unique for given `z`) fixes the form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h2Trace_rossoJones_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h2Trace_rossoJones_odd","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L203-L209","doc":"**Torus knots `τ(2, s)`, `s` odd**: the block's formula\n`[r+1] q^{s(r−1)} − [r−1] q^{s(r−3)}` at `r = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h2Trace_rossoJones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h2Trace_rossoJones","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L193-L201","doc":"**Rosso–Jones at `r = 2`, every `s`**: `[2]² · tr_M(σˢ) = [3] qˢ + (−q⁻¹)ˢ`.\nThe weights are `d_(2)/[2]² = [3]/[2]²` and `d_(1,1)/[2]² = [1]/[2]²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h2Pow_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h2Pow_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L180-L191","doc":"`σ` acts on its two eigenlines by `q` and `−q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h2Trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h2Trace","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L177-L178","doc":"The Markov trace on `H₂(q)`: `tr(1) = 1`, `tr(σ) = z_D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h2Pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h2Pow","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L170-L175","doc":"Coordinates `(a, b)` of `σˢ = a + bσ` in `H₂(q)`, basis `{1, σ}`.\nMultiplying `a + bσ` by `σ` and using `σ² = (q − q⁻¹)σ + 1` gives\n`b + (a + (q − q⁻¹) b) σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hookContent_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hookContent_hook","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L144-L166","doc":"**Two-row hook `(m,1)`, `m ≥ 1`** (so `r = m+1`): first-row cells have\ncontents `0,…,m−1` and hooks `m+1` (corner) then `m−1,…,1`; the second-row cell\nhas content `−1` and hook `1`. Denominators cleared, `d_(m,1) = [m]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hookContent_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hookContent_row","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L131-L142","doc":"**One-row shape `(r)`**: contents `0,…,r−1`, hooks `r,…,1`. The hook-content\nproduct, denominators cleared, gives `d_(r) = [r+1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.prod_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.prod_shift","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L122-L129","doc":"Telescoping core: `∏_{i<r} [i+2] = [r+1] · ∏_{i<r} [i+1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markovZD_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markovZD_eq","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L112-L118","doc":"The block's `z = q²/[2]` is `z_D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markovZD","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L109-L110","doc":"Convention-D Markov parameter `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.qIntBal_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.qIntBal_three","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L101-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.qIntBal_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.qIntBal_two","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L95-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.qIntBal_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.qIntBal_one","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/rj_canonical_inner_product.lean#L90-L93","signatureChunk":0}]}